#HELPS

0 REPEAT AURASHOT CRIPPLE STUNFIST MONKATTACKS~
Syntax: repeat|aurashot|cripple|stunfist <target>
Monk Techs required: Repeat 1, Aura Shot 2, Cripple 5, Stun Fist 7.
REPEAT checks for at least 1200 mana, then spends 600 per repeated hit
while sufficient mana remains. It is not an unlimited free attack.
AURASHOT costs 2000 mana and performs its native life-stealing strike.
CRIPPLE costs 2000 mana and burns the target's mana, bounded at zero.
STUNFIST costs 5000 mana for the native damaging interruption.
These retain native target, safety and resistance checks.
Use the full command AURASHOT or STUNFIST, not ambiguous old labels.
~

0 BLITZ DARKBLAZE MONKAREAATTACKS~
Monk Techs: BLITZ requires 3 and 5000 mana.
It performs the native room-area attack against eligible targets.
DARKBLAZE <target> requires 6 and 2000 mana and attempts native
blindness/disruption on the selected target.
Native combat, safety and resistance rules still apply.
~

0 INVITE MONKPOSSESSION~
Syntax: invite <creature>
Requires Monk Techs 4. Attempts the native weak-creature possession.
The eligible creature's level is limited by your combined Tech, Art
and Mantra ratings; this is not unrestricted player or staff control.
Use the normal RETURN command to leave a successfully borrowed body.
~

0 CHIMERA MONKFORM~
Syntax: chimera
Requires Monk Techs 8. Toggles the native Chimera combat form.
It uses the existing polymorph/form system and is not an additional
standalone parent class or a permanent base-stat increase.
Related: MONKLEARN, WWUPKEEP, UPKEEP.
~

0 TOUCH MONKHEALING~
Syntax: touch [target]
Requires Monk Mantra 4 and a reserve of at least 5000 mana.
With no target, heals the caster; otherwise targets a creature here.
Healing scales with Mantra and is capped at maximum health. The
actual mana cost uses the native healing-cost calculation, checked
before payment; the 5000-mana reserve is not a guaranteed flat fee.
~

0 ALMIGHTY MONKBLESSING~
Syntax: almighty <target>
        almighty group
Requires Monk Mantra 5. The single-target blessing costs 5000 mana;
the group variant costs 20000 mana.
It applies the native blessing to eligible targets, with the existing
duplicate/protection checks. It does not permanently change base stats.
~

0 CELESTIAL MONKTRAVEL~
Syntax: celestial <target>
Requires Monk Mantra 7. The native successful journey costs 1500 mana.
The target must be elsewhere and eligible for Celestial Path; players
must permit summoning. Private/solitary/no-teleport locations cannot be
used to bypass room protection. Both rooms must permit travel; combat,
restraint, roots/curses/webs and incompatible planes block the journey.
Insufficient mana fails without moving you or creating negative mana.
This command relocates the caster, not the selected target.
~

0 LIFECLOAK MONKDEATHWARD~
Syntax: lifecloak
Requires Monk Mantra 8 and completely full health and mana.
Activating the native life-cloak ward reduces current health to 80%
and spends all current mana. It uses the engine's MORE_CLOAK death
protection; it is not general immunity to administrative commands.
The ward cannot be freely stacked or activated while already injured.
~

0 MCLAN DECIDE EXPEL MONKCLANS~
MCLAN lists online members of your Monk clan with current resources.
DECIDE <target> inducts an unclanned Monk here; the caster must meet
the legacy generation gate of 3 or lower. The new member receives
generation 4 and the caster's clan, and both records are saved.
EXPEL <target> removes a Monk of the caster's clan; generation 2 or
lower is required. This is not the future ClassLeader permission model.
These commands do not enroll a character into a hybrid.
~

0 MONKARMOR MONKEQUIPMENT~
Syntax: monkarmor <necklace|habit|belt|tiger|dragon>
Creates eligible native Monk class equipment for 400 quest points
and 100 primal per item. The native object template must exist.
An equipment purchase is not pure-class ascension or hybrid conversion.
Related: MONK, MONKLEARN.
~

